From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maggie Chen <magchen@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:09:18 -0700
Subject: [agy][cc] Use offsets in ListContainerHelper and remove
 RAW_PTR_EXCLUSION InnerList* last_list_

Refactor internal allocator pointers in ListContainerHelper to use
integer offsets instead of raw pointers. Specifically:
- Remove `last_list_` raw pointer in `CharAllocator`, accessing the
  current inner list via `last_list_index_` into `storage_`. This
  avoids dangling pointers when `storage_` reallocates.
- Replace `item_iterator` raw pointer in `PositionInCharAllocator` with
  `item_offset`, eliminating internal raw pointers into allocator
  buffers and deriving `item()` dynamically.

Fixed: 549161451
Test: cc_unittests --gtest_filter="*ListContainer*"
Change-Id: Icec54f062630ee4cc6493c12deb89b8844958c50
Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8452585
Reviewed-by: Vasiliy Telezhnikov <vasilyt@chromium.org>
Commit-Queue: Maggie Chen <magchen@chromium.org>
Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1708319}

